Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sun May 3 08:44:53 2026 +1000

    Switch Ubuntu Erlang source from Launchpad PPA to rabbitmq.com mirror.
    
    Kolla pulls Erlang 27 for Ubuntu image builds from the
    ``rabbitmq-erlang`` PPA on Launchpad (ppa.launchpadcontent.net).
    Launchpad outages have repeatedly broken Debian/Ubuntu image
    builds at the apt-get update step.
    
    The RabbitMQ team publishes the same Erlang packages at
    ``https://deb1.rabbitmq.com/rabbitmq-erlang/ubuntu/noble``, signed
    by the same ``RabbitMQ Release Signing Key`` (key ID
    ``6B73A36E6026DFCA``) that the existing ``rabbitmq-server`` apt
    repo already uses. Switching the ``ubuntu.erlang`` entry in
    ``kolla/template/repos.yaml`` to the rabbitmq.com mirror lets us
    reuse the existing ``rabbitmq.gpg`` keyring with no new key
    material in the base image.
    
    The ``erlang-ppa`` entry in ``base_apt_keys`` is dropped because
    nothing uses it any more -- the prior Debian-side cleanup removed
    the only other reference. After this change Kolla has no
    build-time dependency on Launchpad.
    
    Prompt: Given the launchpadd PPA is down, is there an alternative
    source for these Erlang packages that Ubuntu needs that might be more
    reliable?
    
