index 000000000..5f4326510
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/ubuntu-erlang-from-rabbitmq-mirror-57f9bbe9c37009d1.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+---
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    The ``kolla-toolbox`` and ``rabbitmq`` images on Ubuntu now pull
+    Erlang from the RabbitMQ team's own Debian/Ubuntu mirror at
+    ``https://deb1.rabbitmq.com/rabbitmq-erlang/ubuntu/noble`` instead
+    of the ``rabbitmq-erlang`` PPA hosted on Launchpad
+    (``ppa.launchpadcontent.net``). The mirror ships the same Erlang
+    27.x packages and is signed by the existing
+    ``RabbitMQ Release Signing Key`` (key ID ``6B73A36E6026DFCA``)
+    that the ``rabbitmq-server`` repo already uses, so no new GPG key
+    is added to the base image.
+
+    The now-unused ``erlang-ppa`` keyring entry has been removed from
+    ``base_apt_keys`` in the base Dockerfile, eliminating Kolla's
+    last build-time dependency on Launchpad.
